t.card(p,'01-M01 01-M02 02 03','Define price elasticity of demand (2). Identify supply as elastic or inelastic for coefficients 2 and 0.4 respectively (2). Explain one possible total-revenue effect of a small price rise with inelastic demand and unchanged other demand conditions (2). Identify the percentage changes used in this supplied working: price N$10 to N$11 gives 10%; quantity 100 to 95 gives −5% (2).','PED measures percentage quantity-demanded responsiveness to an own-price change. PES2 is elastic; PES0.4 is inelastic. With locally inelastic demand a small price rise can raise revenue as the quantity reduction is proportionately smaller. The supplied changes are price +10% and quantity −5%.',['Meaning (2): responsiveness of quantity demanded (1), percentage Q change divided by percentage price change (1). Separate points for supply types (2): elastic (1), inelastic (1). Explanation (2): smaller proportional quantity loss (1), price gain can raise revenue under stated conditions (1). Identifications (2): price+10% (1), quantity−5% (1). Marks allocation 8.'])
